      "minDuration": 18,
      "narration": "Now let us arrange 2 by 3, 1 by 6, 5 by 9 and 7 by 12 in ascending order. That means smallest first. The LCM of 3, 6, 9 and 12 is 36. So we get 24 by 36, 6 by 36, 20 by 36 and 21 by 36. Clearly, 6 is the smallest, then 20, then 21, then 24. So the ascending order is 1 by 6, 5 by 9, 7 by 12, 2 by 3.",
